Here's a simple Java program that prints "Hello, World!" to the console:

```java
public class HelloWorld {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello, World!");
    }
}
```

### Explanation:
- `public class HelloWorld`: This defines a class named `HelloWorld`.
- `public static void main(String[] args)`: This is the entry point of any Java application.
- `System.out.println("Hello, World!");`: This line prints "Hello, World!" to the console.
